stance in a faster  way  that's evolution in light speed mode  transitioning from a singular being into  a swarm species that have a better  chance of survival as they always say  two heads are better than one and a  swarm is even more effective  this type of evolution emphasized more  on numbers than on size  godzilla also could physically shift his  body and method of attack based on his  aggressors as well as a personal need as  depicted in the movie for example he  acquired his mouth and dorsal base rays  when humanity's troops successfully  attacked from above with bunker busters  that was the evolution of a ranged  attack to counter faraway targets the  atomic breath godzilla's ability to  shoot his atomic breath from his tail  allowed him pinpoint accuracy while the  spinal rays were for cluster defense  unlike his initial usage he was also  able to do it without expending his  energy or requiring a period of rest  implying that he had evolved to spend  less energy and fight longer for  survival  shin godzilla would have continued to  evolve to counter any incoming threat to  his survival he would have had the  ability of flight with wings and  ultimately becoming a cosmic monster in  the end as theorized in the concept  so next let's look at another version of  the king of the monsters and that is his  anime version godzilla singular point  which also had four forms in total this  iteration of him was quite different  from origin to his final defeat  godzilla in his show was born out of a  trans-dimensional material called the  archetype actually he had been in  existence for millennia as he had  interacted with people in the past and  there was a skeleton of him  his previous self hidden in a vault  so godzilla in this series a closely  followed the same principle of  hyper-evolution as that of shin's  version but here the evolution factor  wasn't his cells  but the archetype interdimensional  molecule that he over time learned to  control and manipulate  in the show he first appeared in 2030 as  an aquatic monster dub as a quarterless  he was first seen 900 meters below the  sea and then later in the same form  chasing a group of mantas which were  headed inland for some reason  after a fight with one of them he  quickly realized that he needed to  change his body quickly in order to suit  with the terrestrial environment he then  became amphibia which although better  suited to live on land was still slow  and clumsy this led him to further  evolve into terrestrials which looks  like a gigantic theropod dinosaur  godzilla expels massive amount of  archetype form his skin in the form of a  crimson dust in all of his four forms  forming a dense cloud around him  and what that is is up to debate but we  can clearly see the red dust being used  as some sort of a terraforming element  as well as a substance to further his  evolution into the perfect life form  designed to survive anything in the  world any threat that he would face  the same as shin this godzilla also  evolves defense mechanisms as well as  attack powers to further his ability to  survive and be dominant  for instance amphibia can breathe a  flammable vapor that is minus 20 degrees  celsius that if ignited the vapor  creates a massive explosion about 500  meters tall  following that he freezes in place his  skin becomes a charcoal black in color  it is stated that in this form it is  just a temporary effect like a chrysalis  in order to protect himself from the  outside environment another example is  terrestris after being hit by bombs  immediately reconfigures the red dust  archetype around him to form some sort  of blood tentacles in order to protect  himself from second rounds of bombs  headed his way they actually became  tentacles and grabbed one of the bombs  mid-air  in the fourth form ultima  it also showed a couple of evolutionary  characteristics  one is his skin becoming super durable  being able to withstand any form of  conventional weaponry as his body has  learned the effect of explosions and how  to counteract them  second is his size he was 45 meters tall  at the start and then at the end he grew  to be a hundred meters tall even his  atomic breath shows his adaptive  behavior and ranged attacks at first his  atomic breath was kind of like a halo  that the third form terrestrials created  and although it was weak it could still  kill a black rodan coming its way the  atomic breath also increased in power  with the fourth form  in his first display then progressively  when he fought off the manda and lastly  when he was fighting off jet jaguar  now let's look at the monsterverse  godzilla how his evolutionary ability  helped him along in the fight against  other titans as well as retaining the  alpha status here in this version we  have nature's benign protector the one  who maintains order embodied in titanus  gojira but how did he become this and  how he changed over time is why we're  here to discuss in the eevee legends of  the novelization it was said that gojira  was like any normal titan but he ate a  hollow earth power souls which they said  it was a star and evolved into something  greater one that was capable of shooting  rays of the star from his mouth which is  the atomic breath  this also gave him the ability to grow  in size as well as change his dorsal  plates after they had shattered in the  fight against demuto prime in 2014  although most of us godzilla didn't show  any fast signs of mutation or  transformation  the changes he had in size power of his  atomic breath and dorsal plates were all  because of his nature to transform into  a more powerful version in order to deal  with more dangerous threats around him  that is evolution or  rather the biological arms race between  species in science it is called the red  queen hypothesis  what is this well the red queen  hypothesis is a theory in evolutionary  biology proposed in 1973  that species must constantly adapt  evolve and pro